mt7601Uap.patch: builds the access point part of github.com/openipc/mt7601u (commit 0ac46553, the
station driver of OpenIPC) as mt7601Uap.ko for wifi-ap. Apply in that source tree with "patch -p1";
build-mt7601Uap.sh does everything. GPL-2.0, like the driver.

- Makefile: an AP-only module (CONFIG_AP_SUPPORT; no station, cfg80211 or ATE code), interface ra0
- include/os/rt_linux.h: the profile is /tmp/mt7601ap/RT2870AP.dat (wifi-ap writes it before ra0
  goes up and deletes it right after)
- the other files: code that the AP-only configuration did not compile (parts that need cfg80211,
  the station driver or dynamic PD are left out)

